if Chrome is so good why do people still  use Firefox well there's actually  several legitimate reasons for this  starting with the computational  requirements it may not seem like it but  Chrome is actually rather  computationally intense and thus is not  very helpful for devices with lower  specs moving on from performance related  benefits we have privacy benefits it's  no secret that Google makes most of  their money by collecting your data and  serving relevant ads Firefox on the  other hand is a non-profit and doesn't  track your browsing history by default  Firefox also blocks cookies and they  generally have substantially better  privacy features than Google given that  they don't have anything to gain from  making these policies loose now it  should be noted that Firefox does not  wipe out data collection altogether if  you go to google.com on Firefox Google  can still collect a bunch of data but if  you use Firefox in combination with  something like duckduckgoa then you'll  actually have a chance at protecting  your privacy
 

